SUMMARY:How We Hear India
DESCRIPTION:\nWhy does a melody move us? \nThis interactive session explores how rhythm\, words\, and the human voice shape the way we experience music\, drawing on the book Band Baaja Bhava: A Musical Journey Across India. Through musical demonstrations\, familiar tunes\, and audience sing-alongs\, it begins with bhava (emotion and expression) and rasa (the aesthetic experience evoked by art)\, inviting listeners into the melody itself. \nThe session moves between live music and discourse\, with the audience taking part throughout. A conversation follows on the ideas and experiences behind the book. Whether you are a lifelong music aficionado or curious to learn about why music moves us\, this is an invitation to listen\, participate\, and discover India through its many musical genres. \n\n\nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nMusic\, Meaning and Emotion\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdQxpHkLH087D8Z0PPLr91lrq855hLhdo_9gRR46Sco5EFIZw/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Chitra Srikrishna\, Sadhana Rao\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Music
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/how-we-hear-india/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Thumbnailbbb.jpg
